{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/763020-need-help-refining-ritual-magic-for-changeling","id":763020,"title":"Need help refining Ritual Magic for Changeling.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T05:31:36-08:00","id":763020,"title":"Need help refining Ritual Magic for Changeling.","content":"So I was reading a thread started by Neo Tiamat talking about his homebrew Wyrd Binding and decided to try and adapt it to something a bit more narrow and defined. I'm hoping you guys out there can look over it and give me some tips and advice.<br /> <br /> The link for the original idea is down below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T05:34:50-08:00","id":763024,"title":"","content":"<u>Ritual Magic:</u><br /> The fae of story are described as having wondrous powers; spinning straw into gold, binding domains with impossible riddles and even animating objects to act as servants. But while most of these abilities can be found in the confines of contracts, many more are left without a counterpart. Some would say that these are the powers that belong solely to the Gentry, but isn\u2019t the centre of their power the ability to strike bargains?<br /> It was with that question in mind that Changelings set about learning-or perhaps relearning-many of the abilities spoken of in story. These were beyond contracts, they both more and less. By striking oaths with certain aspects of reality, with the nature of story, changelings are able to enact wonders beyond the reach of pledges.<br /> <br /> <u>How it works:</u><br /> When enacting a ritual the changeling must first know what they want the ritual to do. Do they want to bind an abstraction? Deliver a message? Ward a household?<br /> <br /> Second, they must decide an appropriate Wyrd purview to call upon. The changeling must be in the presence of this purview in order to call upon it-they can call upon stone in a quarry, or they could try and bind twilight during sunrise or sunset. But not bind sunlight in a windowless room.<br /> <br /> The third step is striking the bargain. Here you must ask the Wyrd to help you, offering a price. This works the same way as if you were pledge crafting, only you don\u2019t have to specify a sanction as the Wyrd will level its own if you renege on your end of the deal. You must also perform whatever task or boon you say you will alongside whatever preparations you make for the ritual.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of this step is the ritual act. It is this that separates ritual magic from Contracts or Goblin vows. You must perform actions that bestow a sense of gravitas to the pledge. This can be as simple as singing a song or carving a symbol of your own making, to something as complex as anointing a statue with the blood of seven newborns on the night of a blue moon. The complexity of the ritual must be commensurate with the task being asked for-to trap a tornado in a bottle, one would need to perform a ritual on par with the great mystical ceremonies found across the world.<br /> <br /> It is in the ritual that the risk enters. Though the ritual may not be innately imbued with power, the fact that a changeling is using it to commune with the Wyrd grants it power, if only for that one occasion. This means that the Wyrd has certain expectations of the Changeling, it expects them to be shamans, wizards, mystics in tune with the deep workings of the universe because that\u2019s the part they are attempting to play. To that effect, the changeling must role their Wyrd score to represent whether or not the Wyrd accepts them in the part. Modifiers based on the effort put into the ritual may increase the likelihood of the ritual working. It\u2019s an instant role with a target number of success based on the complexity of the task being requested.<br /> <br /> However, autumn changelings, with their innate affinity for magic, also gain a bonus based on their Mantle: +1 at one dot; +2 at three dots; +3 at five dots.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}